    <!-- Help screen: model guide (aligned with models/README.md) -->
    <string name="help_section_model_pick">Choosing a model</string>
    <string name="help_scenario_anime">Anime / Illustration / Game screenshots</string>
    <string name="help_scenario_anime_desc">Start with Real-ESRGANv3-anime for fast, clean lines. For heavy compression noise (older anime, streaming captures), use Real-CUGAN pro denoise variants. For crisp 4x lines, pick AnimeSharp-x4; for heavily degraded sources, pick HFA2k-x4. HFA2k-LUDVAE-SPAN-x2 is the lightest anime restoration model, and ModernSpanimation-x2 steps up quality for modern animation.</string>
    <string name="help_scenario_photo_2x">Photos · Light upscale (x2)</string>
    <string name="help_scenario_photo_2x_desc">NomosUni-Compact-x2 is trained for compressed chat and social-media photos and runs fast locally on phone batches. Parimg-Compact-x2 is also lightweight with stronger cleanup. For reference quality, choose Real-ESRGAN-x2plus (PC recommended).</string>
    <string name="help_scenario_photo_4x">Photos · Large upscale (x4)</string>
    <string name="help_scenario_photo_4x_desc">For speed on phone, pick Real-ESRGANv3-general-x4 or LSDIR-Compact-v2-x4. For maximum detail (PC recommended), use NomosWebPhoto-RealPLKSR, Nomos2-OTF, BSRGAN, Remacri, UltraSharp, or Real-ESRGAN-x4plus.</string>
    <string name="help_scenario_restore">Native resolution restore (1x, no upscale)</string>
    <string name="help_scenario_restore_desc">Use when resolution is already right and only artifacts need cleanup: DeJPG / DeNoise / DeH264-RealPLKSR-x1 target JPEG blocks, sensor noise, and video compression for photos; Archivist-Medium (balanced) or Archivist-Rough (heavy damage) target anime and video frames; NES-Composite-RGB and Genesis-Cleanup handle retro console composite artifacts. Keeps original dimensions and runs faster than any upscaler.</string>
    <string name="help_model_tips_title">Tips</string>
    <string name="help_model_tip_scale">Scale follows the model: the x1 / x2 / x3 / x4 suffix sets the scale (x1 restores at native size). The scale toggle only switches variants within the same model family.</string>
    <string name="help_model_tip_weight">Lightweight 1–2 MB models run effortlessly on-device in batches. Heavy 31 MB models deliver higher texture fidelity and run much faster when offloaded to a PC.</string>
    <string name="help_model_tip_get">Models are not bundled with the app: download them from Models or the model picker sheet, or import your own .param / .bin files.</string>
    <string name="help_section_model_families">Model families</string>
    <string name="help_family_v3">Real-ESRGAN v3 · Fast all-rounders</string>
    <string name="help_family_v3_desc">Compact 1–2 MB networks fast enough for mobile batches: the anime series is the default pick for anime, and general-x4 is the default pick for photos.</string>
    <string name="help_family_x4plus">Real-ESRGAN x4plus · Heavy reference quality</string>
    <string name="help_family_x4plus_desc">Full RRDB networks with the strongest texture reconstruction in the catalog, at tens of times the compute cost—best used with PC offload. x4plus-anime is the 4x anime reference, and x2plus brings the same recipe to 2x when lightweight 2x models fall short.</string>
    <string name="help_family_cugan">Real-CUGAN · Anime specialist</string>
    <string name="help_family_cugan_desc">Trained for real-world anime degradation; often beats Real-ESRGAN on heavily compressed JPEG or video frames. Three variants: conservative (minimal alteration), denoise (strong compression noise removal), and no-denoise. Prefer the newer pro line for better generalization.</string>
    <string name="help_family_photo">Community photo models · Nomos &amp; more</string>
    <string name="help_family_photo_desc">Photo-focused models filling gaps around Real-ESRGAN: NomosUni-Compact-x2 and Parimg-Compact-x2 are fast 2x photo models (Parimg cleans harder); SPAN-x4 is the lightest; LSDIR-Compact-v2-x4 is cleaner at similar speed; Nomos8kSC-x4 removes heavier compression and blur; Nomos2-OTF-x4 uses a newer real-world degradation pipeline; NomosWebPhoto-RealPLKSR-x4 balances quality and size for web photos.</string>
    <string name="help_family_restore">Native resolution restore · 1x</string>
    <string name="help_family_restore_desc">Same-size restoration models, faster than any upscaler: DeJPG / DeNoise / DeH264-RealPLKSR-x1 (14 MB) remove JPEG blocking, noise, and video compression on photos; Archivist-Medium / Rough-Compact-x1 (0.6 MB, MIT) clean film grain and wear on anime and video frames; NES-Composite-RGB / Genesis-Cleanup (4 MB, MIT) clean retro console composite captures.</string>
    <string name="help_family_classics">Community classics · UltraSharp / Remacri / BSRGAN</string>
    <string name="help_family_classics_desc">Long-standing general favorites: UltraSharp-x4 (crisp), Remacri-x4 (natural), AnimeSharp-x4 (sharp 4x anime lines), AnimeJaNai-v2-Compact-x2 (lightweight 2x anime), NMKD-Siax-x4 (texture preservation), and BSRGAN-x4/x2 (academic multi-degradation baseline, Apache-2.0). Note: except NMKD (WTFPL) and BSRGAN (Apache-2.0), the other four carry non-commercial licenses (CC-BY-NC-SA), which do not restrict personal use.</string>
    <string name="home_model_picker_help">Not sure which to pick? Read the model guide</string>

